// Native canonical-IPA data manifest for Hmong (hmn) — White Hmong / Hmoob Dawb (Hmong Daw, mww), Hmong-Mien,
// tonal, ~8M (SW China / SE Asia / diaspora). Consumed by hmong.ts. Input = the Romanized Popular Alphabet (RPA),
// the community-standard phonemic Latin orthography (Barney-Smalley, 1953). RPA has NO coda consonants → a word-final
// consonant letter is ALWAYS a TONE marker (b j v s g m d; no letter = mid tone). The converter: onset (longest
// multigraph match) + rime + tone-letter → IPA. ⟨tx x⟩ PALATALISE to [t͡ɕ ɕ] before /i/. Rich onset system:
// prenasalised (np→ᵐb, nts→ᶯd͡ʐ), voiceless sonorants (hm→m̥, hl→l̥), retroflex (r→ʈ, ts→t͡ʂ), uvular (q). Maps derived
// from the wikipron mww_latn_broad referee (~470 pairs) + the documented RPA tables. Nasal vowels ⟨ee oo⟩→[ẽ ɒ̃].
// See docs/investigations/hmn_native_bringup_investigation.md.
